From cc296ed5cfafa64b2d5887d3aef75e284c445c86 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Will Eaton <weaton@redhat.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 10:51:55 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] [Core] Release weights for a process checkpoint with
 --checkpoint-release-weights

With --checkpoint-release-weights, /checkpoint/prepare also discards the
weights after the KV cache, so a process checkpoint does not contain them,
and /checkpoint/restore wakes the weights and refills them through the
model loader before the KV cache. A checkpoint of a large model then stays
small, and a loader such as ModelExpress can refill the weights from a
running peer through reload_weights_inplace.

Worker.discard(("weights",)) now does what a level-2 sleep does for the
weights: it calls the loader's on_sleep(2) and saves the buffers and the
retained parameters, which wake_up(["weights"]) restores.
